      "description": "Watch FK Jablonec vs Rangers highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 27, 2026. A high-stakes UEFA Conference League encounter between FK Jablonec and Rangers delivered a night of immense drama and tactical intrigue. Neither side was willing to give an inch in a match that tested the physical and mental limits of every player on the pitch. Tight Contest and Tactical Adjustments On August 27, 2026 , the match kicked off with both teams looking to establish dominance in the middle of the park. The early stages were physical, evidenced by a yellow card for Martin Cedidla in the 18th minute. As the first half ended goalless, Rangers opted for a triple substitution at the restart, bringing on Lawrence Shankland , Findlay Curtis , and Connor Barron to provide a fresh attacking impetus. The changes shifted the momentum, but the Czech defense remained resolute. Breakthrough and Extra Time Tension The deadlock was finally broken in the 73rd minute when Vakhtang Tchanturishvili found the target for FK Jablonec , sending the home fans into a frenzy. Rangers fought back valiantly to equalize and send the tie into extra time. The additional period was characterized by tired legs and rising tensions, resulting in yellow cards for Antonin Rusek and Lawrence Shankland . Despite tactical tweaks and the introduction of Bojan Miovski and Thelo Aasgaard , the scoreline remained unchanged after 120 minutes of play. Penalty Shoot-out Drama The pressure reached its peak during the penalty shoot-out. FK Jablonec saw successful strikes from Jan Chramosta , Nelson Okeke , Richard Sedlacek , and Antonin Rusek , while Filip Zorvan missed his attempt. For Rangers , the shootout proved to be their undoing as James Penrice and Findlay Curtis both missed from the spot. Although Thelo Aasgaard , Bojan Miovski , and Lawrence Shankland converted their penalties, it was Jablonec who celebrated a hard-fought victory."
