      "description": "Watch Rangers vs FK Jablonec highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 20, 2026. The UEFA Conference League action returned with a high-stakes encounter between Rangers and FK Jablonec . Both teams entered the pitch with everything to play for, creating an atmosphere of anticipation and nervous energy among the supporters. Defensive Discipline in the Opening Period On August 20, 2026 , the match began with a tactical chess match as both sides prioritized defensive stability. Rangers looked to control the tempo, but FK Jablonec proved to be a stubborn opponent. The physical nature of the contest was established early on when Emmanuel Fernandez received a yellow card in the 11th minute. Despite several half-chances, neither side could find the breakthrough before the referee blew for half-time, leaving the tactical battle finely poised. Naderi Finds the Net The deadlock was finally broken shortly after the restart. In the 50th minute, Daisuke Yokota delivered a pinpoint assist into the path of Ryan Don Naderi , who made no mistake in front of goal to spark wild celebrations in the stands. Following the goal, FK Jablonec attempted to change their fortunes with a double substitution, bringing on Hugo Ahl and Filip Zorvan . Rangers seemed to be in command, but the game was far from over. Red Card Chaos and Late Pressure The momentum shifted dramatically in the 78th minute when Cameron Devlin was shown a straight red card. The decision triggered heavy protests from the Rangers players, but the hosts were forced to play the remainder of the match with ten men. FK Jablonec pushed forward in search of an equalizer, with Hugo Ahl and Richard Sedlacek both picking up bookings in a frantic finale. However, despite six minutes of added time and intense pressure, the home side held firm to secure a vital victory."
